{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/193447-use-of-the-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-allied-pantheon","id":193447,"title":"Use of the Atlantean Pantheon and the Allied Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-10T06:10:56-07:00","id":193447,"title":"Use of the Atlantean Pantheon and the Allied Pantheon","content":"So, how many of you have used the Atlantean pantheon and the allied pantheon in play? I know there's a general consensus on this board that the Atlantean pantheon and the allied pantheons are badly done and not very useful. BUT, they are still intriguing to me, so how have you used them and how did it turn out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T07:31:47-07:00","id":193548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gemstone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/193447-use-of-the-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-allied-pantheon#post193447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there's a general consensus on this board that the Atlantean pantheon and the allied pantheons are badly done and not very useful. BUT, they are still intriguing to me, so how have you used them and how did it turn out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that Atlantean pantheon is pretty well done. The problem is that they are complete fiction with no history or claim to legitimacy like the primary pantheons.<br /> <br /> I have had some good times playing in a game where Paul Bunyan was a giant, and most of the allied pantheons were all low legend scions of real gods (except Britannia, who was actually legend 9).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T08:17:03-07:00","id":193637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/193447-use-of-the-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-allied-pantheon?p=193548#post193548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that Atlantean pantheon is pretty well done. The problem is that they are complete fiction with no history or claim to legitimacy like the primary pantheons.<br /> <br /> I have had some good times playing in a game where Paul Bunyan was a giant, and most of the allied pantheons were all low legend scions of real gods (except Britannia, who was actually legend 9).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah... if they only had allowed gods to pass on purviews and such from the lowest legend (9 irrc) they would've solved everything... I'm really fond of the idea of the allied pantheon all being scions of the older pantheons. It makes so much thematical sense.<br /> <br /> I mean, I can practically see Uncle Sam as a legend 9 Scion of Zeus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:21:35-07:00","id":193697,"title":"","content":"I just borrowed the idea of there being a collection of the children of gods of different pantheons that may or may not have been able to break away from their parents enough to form a sorta-American (meaning USA) pantheon. The only one the characters had any dealing with was Columbia (daughter of Athena) and they had no idea whether she was Legend 9 or Legend 12 or somewhere in between. One of the tensions in the game was &quot;European immigrants&quot; vs. &quot;Native American pantheons already in place&quot; and that situation was being exploited by some Titanspawn and Titan minions who were trying to allow their masters to walk the world. <br /> <br /> They got some info on some other members of the &quot;pantheon&quot;. They all seemed pretty estranged.<br /> <br /> Never used the Atlantean pantheon. Consider it salvage for spare parts to integrate elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:42:06-07:00","id":193713,"title":"","content":"Creating a pantheon was always interesting to me. I'd look at the older <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Indo-European_religion\" target=\"_blank\">proto-Indo-European deities</a> and even older <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paleolithic_Religion\" target=\"_blank\">timesframes</a> and just let my imagination fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:48:25-07:00","id":193730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/193447-use-of-the-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-allied-pantheon?p=193697#post193697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just borrowed the idea of there being a collection of the children of gods of different pantheons that may or may not have been able to break away from their parents enough to form a sorta-American (meaning USA) pantheon. The only one the characters had any dealing with was Columbia (daughter of Athena) and they had no idea whether she was Legend 9 or Legend 12 or somewhere in between. One of the tensions in the game was &quot;European immigrants&quot; vs. &quot;Native American pantheons already in place&quot; and that situation was being exploited by some Titanspawn and Titan minions who were trying to allow their masters to walk the world.<br /> <br /> They got some info on some other members of the &quot;pantheon&quot;. They all seemed pretty estranged.<br /> <br /> Never used the Atlantean pantheon. Consider it salvage for spare parts to integrate elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually an idea I almost used for our games, but we never got to the point were it got interesting. We trailed off and I put that story aside for some other grand plots. Sounds really awesome though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:50:16-07:00","id":193731,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">American Legends</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Betsy Ross \u2013 Immortal Woman (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Remembered now for sewing the first American Flag in 1776, Betsy Ross was otherwise an unassuming woman. Now historians doubt that she even performed the single deed that garnered her fame. True or not, Miss Betsy Ross gained the attention of one of the few Scions walking the World in the 18th century. She was a hard worker and she survived a life full of many trials. Something about her spurred the Scion to grant her a gift. Ross is blind, old and fragile, but she is most certainly alive. She has almost three hundred years of experience and knowledge to bestow on young Scions, though her viewpoints are a little old fashioned.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Br\u2019er Rabbit \u2013 Trickster Avatar</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">No one is sure </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">exactly</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> who Br\u2019er Rabbit is, because there are many Br\u2019er Rabbits. The name and form of the old Southern trickster are worn by many different Gods dropping by the Deep South for a visit. Sometimes he is a regular hare that acts in extraordinary ways, other times he is an anthropomorphic rabbit who walks about upright, wearing trousers and a collared shirt. He\u2019s even appeared as an old country man with buck teeth, a harelip and too-big ears. Some suspects for Br\u2019er Rabbit include Coyote, Anansi and even Loki. Most commonly he is assumed to be either a West African or a Native American deity assuming a more modern guise. Sometimes Br\u2019er Rabbit helps Scions, but he\u2019s just as likely to be stirring up the trouble that has drawn Scions to the area in the first place. You just never know.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Columbia \u2013 Minor Goddess (Guide 4)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There are conflicting tales of Columbia\u2019s origin and she isn\u2019t clearing them up. Some say she is a daughter of Athena, others say she is an Avatar or aspect of the older Goddess, still others suggest that Columbia is a Titanspawn, possibly a creature of Logos, somehow related to Themis. Whatever her true origin, Columbia presents herself as the Goddess of the United States. She has little respect from more established figures and, in truth, has little power of her own. She has no Scions and, so far as anyone can tell, never has had any. She does take an interest in any Scion who meddles too closely in the affairs of the United States and sometimes appears to guide them onto the \u2018correct\u2019 course for her favored nation. Since the 20\u2019s, Columbia has more and more often appeared as Lady Liberty, often carrying a torch and wearing robes and a crown resembling those on a certain famous copper statue. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">John Henry \u2013 Ghost, Former Scion of Heracles (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Remembered in story and song, John Henry would have been a great Scion if he hadn\u2019t worked himself to death in the earliest stages of his Legend. He is now a ghost and since the breaking of Tartarus, has returned to the World and finds much to his distaste. Too much automation, too much laziness and reliance on machines and mass production instead of hard work and quality. He still has knowledge of strange and Legendary World that Scions inhabit to offer, as well as his own experience.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Johnny Appleseed \u2013 Adopted Legendary Persona (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The real Johnny Appleseed, John Chapman, was an extraordinary mortal man who lived a life that earned him some measure of Legendary status, but in 1845 he died, as mortals do. Chapman had so impressed some of the lesser Immortals and nature spirits of North America that they continue his Legend. Johnny Appleseed appears here and there, a form worn by a variety of nature spirits native to the United States, especially in Pennsylvania, Ohio, Indiana and Illinois. He tends forests, protects animals and encourages preservation. Scions who are attempting to protect nature and its creatures in the areas he frequents can sometimes find Johnny Appleseed and ask for his help. He may even take an extended interest in preservation-inclined Scions in his ranges.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Paul Bunyan \u2013 Earth Giant (Guide 3)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Now known as the archetypical lumberjack, Bunyan\u2019s history goes back much, much further. It goes all the way back to Vinland, where Paul Bunyan was simply a Giant who pursued a Norse Scion across the ocean. The Scion slipped through his grasp, but their fight forced the young Hero to abandon his favorite mount: a blue ox. The ox was taken by Bunyan as a trophy of his victory and became his constant companion. Over time, he acclimated to his home in the New World and grew to care greatly for the earth and forests of Canada and the northern United States. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pecos Bill \u2013 Demigod (Guide 2-3)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A brash Scion from the American West, Pecos Bill\u2019s deeds were enough to earn him the status of Demigod, but never to propel him towards Apotheosis. As the wild west was tamed, Bill slowly withdrew from the World more and more, spending time in several of the Terra Incognitae scattered through the West. Pecos Bill claims to not know who his father was and there are various suspicions cast on figures such as Coyote, Thor, Zeus, Apollo and even Vayu. He still appears sometimes, often drawn out of his adventures in other Worlds by news of Titanspawn causing trouble in his old stomping grounds. He sometimes acts as a Guide for young Heroes, but he always wanders and his attention can be fleeting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rosie the Riveter \u2013 Avatar of Brigit</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Following along with the Irish immigrants to the United States, the Goddess of Flame and Forge came to America and took on a new persona during the Second World War. She became an icon of female power and industrial might. She worked tirelessly to help uplift and empower female workers and inspire bravery and courage in all the descendants of her people, both at home and on the battlefield.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Uncle Sam \u2013 Avatar of Zeus</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The personification of the US government sometimes comes to life and walks the World, encouraging and directing the United States towards greatness. He has another name, one far more famous: Zeus. The King of the Greek Gods was all too pleased with the attention lavished upon the culture he oversaw by the fledgeling nation across the oceans. Sometimes he takes on this identity and connects with the New World in a way slightly more effective than togas and laurels.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">British Legends</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Britannia \u2013 Minor Goddess (Guide 4) </span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once a Scion of Minerva, Britannia was the Goddess of a faraway land that her Empire had set its eyes upon. She embraced the society that she patronized and as Roman influence in England waned, Britannia grew closer to her worshippers and farther away from her divine relatives. She has forged close ties with the native Gods of the British Isles, though she is always a foreigner among them. If young Scions wish her guidance and aid, they must only make clear that they have the best interests of England at heart.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">John Bull \u2013 Hero (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The only known Scion of Britannia, John Bull represents not England as a whole, but the middle class, common sense, salt of the earth people. He has walked among them for decades, locked forever in the form of a portly man just past the prime of life but with many years ahead. He reminds the people of tradition and stability during times of tumult and serves as a beacon of national identity that people can relate to, rather than sharing the remoteness that his mother and other, similar goddesses have about them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Robin Hood \u2013 Demigod (Guide 3)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Scion most recently known as Robin Hood has worn many faces through history. He has been the Green Knight of Arthurian tales and Herne the Hunter who roamed the forests of England. Some claim that he has only played these parts occasionally and that others contributed to the legends. Cernunnos has been suspected of lending to the tale of Herne, but Robin Hood and the Horned God have always been on good terms. It may be that Cernunnos is Robin\u2019s father, but neither is inclined to discuss the matter.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">French Legends</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">d\u2019Artagnan \u2013 Legendary Ghost (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Though he may not know it any longer, d'Artagnan is not the character of fiction created by Alexandre Dumas. He began life as a mortal who became captain of the Musketeers under Louis XIV. His deeds inspired Dumas\u2019 stories and the confused spirit has been captured by the webs of Legend woven around him. He has gone insane under the pressure of Fatebonds, not having the innate resistance to their shaping that true Legendary beings do. He is no longer certain if he was ever alive, and truly believes himself to be the character of Dumas\u2019 stories. While insane, he can offer guidance in certain matters to Scions willing and able to deal with his dementia.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Madame Guillotine \u2013 Avatar of Andarta</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The bloodthirsty Gaulish Goddess of War returned to France during the Revolution and enjoyed the offerings of blood and severed heads. She walked among the French under the guise of Madame Guillotine. Occasionally Andarta still takes on the form of La Terreur, but only rarely. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Marianne \u2013 Demigoddess (Guide 3)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">One of the last Scions of Teutates, Marianne rose from a long-lived Hero to a powerful Demigoddess during the turmoil of the French Revolution. She is one of the few connections between the modern nation of France and its ancient Gaulish heritage and that connection is thin indeed. Marianne fully embraces the modern world and her Gaulish family questions her loyalties. Undaunted, the brave Demigoddess seeks to always support and protect her people and her country.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Russian Legends</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Baba Yaga \u2013 Lesser Immortal (Guide 5)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Little Grandmother of Slavic Folklore is not a Goddess, though she is more powerful than some. She lives in the Dark Forest, in a hut with no door and giant chicken legs that allow it to walk around. Gifts of blue roses can appease her, as can proper manners and heroic deeds. She exacts a great price for her aid, but she is said to know almost everything and she is one of the most powerful sorceresses in Europe.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Citizen \u2013 Legendary Ghost (Guide 2)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once, the Citizen had a name but he no longer does. He died during the Russian Revolution but his death was of no consequence to his mission. He still defends Russia from her enemies. Disembodied and deceased, the ghost\u2019s pure strength of will has allowed him to possess the bodies of mortal Russian soldiers. He has engaged in every conflict Russia has been involved in since his death, fighting bravely and without fear of death. After all, he is already dead and it is the duty of a soldier to lay down his life for his country.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rodina Mat \u2013 Scion of Mokosh (Guide 3)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Daughter of the ancient Slavic Earth Goddess, Rodina Mat (called Mother Russia in English) has abandoned her mortal name and assumed the role of patron for all the Russian people. She encourages fertility of the land, health of the people and distributes fortune and wealth where appropriate. Like other nationalistic figures, she will offer her aid to those who act in the best interests of the nation she favors. Unlike Columbia or Britannia, Rodina Mat is too young to have become a Goddess; she is still a Demigoddess, though one of age and power.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Roman Legends</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Caligula \u2013 Titan-Sworn Scion</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A tyrant during his rule, Caligula was sadistic and capricious. He outraged his father, Jupiter and was cut off from contact with his divine family. Spitefully, the disgraced Scion turned to the Titans and pledged himself to their service. His assassination was faked to remove him from the notice of the Roman Gods. In the pits of Tartarus, he gained dark power and now serves the Titans\u2019 purposes by taking on the role of a Guide to young Greek and Roman Scions, leading them slowly down the path of corruption he himself followed centuries ago.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Quirinus \u2013 Minor God (Guide 5)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Originally a Scion of Mars under the name Remus, the founder of Rome reached Godhood after establishing the foundations of an Empire that would shape the history of the World. He became a figure of civil order and martial prowess. He still lives on Olympus with the other Roman Gods, occasionally mentoring Scions and watching over the descendants of the people he lead to greatness.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:07:02-07:00","id":193834,"title":"","content":"I love those, Telgar! Now we need some from places in South America, Africa, &amp; Asia!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:57:50-07:00","id":194105,"title":"","content":"I'm using the Atlantean Pantheon as a badguys during the return of the Titans. They are back to have revenge on all the other Pantheons for banishing them and destroying their mortal followers (and their entire home land).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T18:26:09-07:00","id":194170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/193447-use-of-the-atlantean-pantheon-and-the-allied-pantheon?p=193731#post193731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Long Awesom Post]</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are great <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really like how you put in the possible parent in some of them too ^^<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-18T00:17:38-07:00","id":200804,"title":"","content":"Long ago my first Scion game ever started as a Highlander game with the atlantean scions as immortals. My version of the atlantean purview (made long before the Companion &amp; Scire) was a set of powers with a thematic of community and sacrifice (similar in some aspects to the Aztec purview), the idea being that many of the peculiarities of immortals and &quot;The Game&quot; were the result of terrible devolution and debasement brought by the destruction of most of the original children of the Atlantean gods, all of the &quot;immortals&quot; being in fact scions of other pantheons &quot;adopted&quot; in near-death experiences through a strange combination of fate-binding and the higher levels of the purview by slumbering, chained gods forgotten by the world for millenia. It started as the highlander for the setting to slowly expand into Scion and stranger &amp; greater challenges, from Scion &amp; Highlander settings both, crossed their paths and slowly lead them to inklings of the long-lost truth and the remaining, demigod level &quot;true atlantean&quot; scions (inspired in Methos and the Horsemen of the TV series and a few others).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately we had to interupt that game right at that point and they were getting <b>really</b> into demigod level and a crazy plan to go to Antartica and free the atlantean gods of their imprisonment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 